.TH mbsvpbest 1 "3 November 2026" "MB-System 5.0" "MB-System 5.0"
.SH NAME
\fBmbsvpbest\fP \- Compare World Ocean Atlas and embedded sound velocity
profiles on swath data over locally planar seafloor.

.SH VERSION
Version 5.0

.SH SYNOPSIS
\fBmbsvpbest\fP
.br
--svpfolder=directory {-Sdirectory}
.br
--apply-best
.br
--enddate {-E}
.br
--help {-H}
.br
--input=file {-Ifile} (also --swathfile)
.br
--minimum-beams=number
.br
--nearest {-N}
.br
--outputfolder=directory {-Odirectory}
.br
--period=period[,period...] {-Pperiod[,period...]}
.br
--plots
.br
--resolution=01|04[,...] {-R01|04[,...]}
.br
--selection=combined|per-file
.br
--verbose {-V}

.SH DESCRIPTION
\fBmbsvpbest\fP compares sound velocity profiles (SVPs) by applying each of
them to swath data through \fBmbprocess\fP and measuring how far the resulting
depths lie from a straight line in each ping. The most recently measured
profile is not always the most representative one for a survey, so the profile
embedded in the swath file is tested as one candidate among the others rather
than taken as a reference.

The candidates are:
.br
\- World Ocean Atlas 2018 and 2023 climatological profiles at the survey, for
the requested periods and resolutions, in annual, seasonal and monthly versions
for the month of the survey, each computed with the Chen and Millero and with the
Leroy sound speed formulas. WOA18 and WOA23 values are never blended.
.br
\- The profiles embedded in the swath files, extracted with \fBmbsvplist\fP.
These must start within 1 m of the surface, reach the maximum depth of the survey,
have strictly increasing depths and speeds between 1200 and 2000 m/s, and are
otherwise rejected with a note. A profile with the same depths and speeds as one
already kept is evaluated only once.

In each ping, depth is fitted by a straight line against acrosstrack distance.
The residuals of all pings and all files are pooled, and the candidates are ranked by
the root mean square of these residuals (RMSE); the lowest finite RMSE
wins, and equal scores keep the candidate order. The mean absolute error, mean square
error, mean error and the sounding and ping counts are reported too.

\fBThe result needs care.\fP The winner is the best of the profiles tested, for the
selected data and this metric. The ranking does not show that it reproduces the
true water column. The metric assumes locally planar seafloor, so use data free of
real relief across the swath. There is no common mask of soundings across candidates: a
candidate that loses difficult outer soundings can gain from it, so compare the
sounding counts and read \fBprofile_notes\fP and \fBcandidate_failures\fP
in the report.

.B Sound speed grids
.br
The program requires at least one of the sound speed datasets posted at
https://zenodo.org/communities/mb-system_woa_svp_datasets/
.br
The directory given with \fB\-\-svpfolder\fP holds these NetCDF files, named
woaYY_PERIOD_svpTT_RR.nc, where YY is 18 or 23, TT is 00 (annual), 01 to 12
(months) or 13 to 16 (seasons), and RR is 01 (1 degree) or 04 (0.25 degree). They
contain the variables v_an_chen and v_an_leroy on the dimensions depth, lat and lon.
Only direct children of the directory that match the requested periods and
resolutions and the month or season of the survey are used.

.B Completion to 11000 m
.br
Invalid samples are removed. A seasonal profile takes deeper valid annual samples,
and a monthly profile takes the deeper seasonal and annual samples, from the same
edition, period and resolution; no value is changed at a join. A profile that is still
short gets an endpoint at 11000 m from a least-squares line through its samples in
the deepest 2000 m of valid coverage. This endpoint is a processing extrapolation,
not an observation. A survey deeper than 11000 m is rejected.

.B Selection modes
.br
With \fB\-\-selection=combined\fP, the default, one profile is chosen for all the input
files. The candidates use the combined bounds of the files, and all files must share the
selected month. With \fB\-\-selection=per-file\fP each file is evaluated on its own with
its own bounds, date, candidates and winner. A file that fails is recorded and the next one
goes on; an interrupt stops the batch.

.B Files
.br
A combined evaluation makes OUTPUTFOLDER/run-DATE-TIME holding the candidate
profiles, ranking.json, ranking.csv and commands.log, the output of the programs run. A
per-file evaluation makes OUTPUTFOLDER/per-file-DATE-TIME with summary.json and a
folder NNNN_NAME/run-DATE-TIME for each input file. The candidates carry their source and
location in comment lines starting with # MBSVPBEST_LOCATION and # MBSVPBEST_DONOR.

During the evaluation \fBmbsvpbest\fP changes the parameter file of each input
file, and \fBmbprocess\fP rewrites its reverse edit save file (.resf) and may leave a
lock file (.lck) if it is stopped. These are put back as they were at the end of the run,
on failure and on an interrupt; copies stay in the backup folder of the run directory
until then, in case the program is killed. Do not run other jobs on the same files at the same time, and try
new settings on copies of the data first. Paths written to a parameter file
cannot contain spaces.

