.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.B \-\-apply-best
Set the winning profile in the parameter files of the input files and process
them with \fBmbprocess\fP. In combined mode the parameter files are put back if any
file fails, but outputs already made stay. In per-file mode each winner is applied right
after its evaluation, so earlier applications stay after a later failure. Processing can
overwrite existing output files: review a ranking first.
.TP
.B \-\-enddate {\-E}
Select the month and season from the end of each file instead of its start.
.TP
.B \-\-help {\-H}
Print a short description and the usage, and exit.
.TP
.B \-\-input=\fIfile\fP {\-I\fIfile\fP}
Swath file or datalist. Nested datalists are allowed, a datalist that includes itself,
a listed file that does not exist and formats below \-1 are errors.
Default: datalist.mb-1. \fB\-\-swathfile\fP is the same option.
.TP
.B \-\-minimum-beams=\fInumber\fP
A ping with fewer valid soundings is left out and counted as rejected. Minimum 3,
default 5.
.TP
.B \-\-nearest {\-N}
Use the profile of the nearest grid cell with valid near-surface coverage, instead of
the mean over the cells that bracket the survey. Only the 16 nearest cells are
examined, with a warning when a neighbour replaces the nearest cell.
.TP
.B \-\-outputfolder=\fIdirectory\fP {\-O\fIdirectory\fP}
Parent directory of the output, made if necessary. Default: svpprofiles.
.TP
.B \-\-period=\fIperiod\fP[,\fIperiod\fP...] {\-P\fIperiod\fP[,\fIperiod\fP...]}
Climatological periods to use, separated by commas or spaces or by repeating the option.
Default: decav, A5B7 and B5C2. Periods that exist for only one edition
are used for that edition.
.TP
.B \-\-plots
For each candidate write a table of the mean, standard deviation and count of the
residuals by beam, and plot it to a PNG file with GMT. A plot that fails gives a
warning and does not stop the evaluation.
.TP
.B \-\-resolution=01|04[,...] {\-R01|04[,...]}
Grid resolutions to use: 01 is 1 degree, 04 is 0.25 degree, separated by commas or
spaces or by repeating the option. Default: both.
.TP
.B \-\-selection=combined|per-file
One winner for all input files (default) or one for each input file.
.TP
.B \-\-svpfolder=\fIdirectory\fP {\-S\fIdirectory\fP}
Directory of the sound speed grids, from the datasets posted at
https://zenodo.org/communities/mb-system_woa_svp_datasets/
Required.
.TP
.B \-\-verbose {\-V}
Print the commands that are run. Repeat for debugging output.

.SH EXIT STATUS
0 on success, 1 on failure (for per-file selection, if any file failed), 9 for wrong
usage and 130 after an interrupt.

.SH EXAMPLES
Compare the decav candidates at 1 degree with the embedded profiles of a set of lines
from the same month, using one profile for all of them:
.br
	mbsvpbest -I datalist.mb-1 -S woa_data -P decav -R 01 -O evaluation

One winner for each line, for all default periods at both resolutions, using the nearest cell:
.br
	mbsvpbest -I datalist.mb-1 -S woa_data -N --selection=per-file -O evaluation

After reviewing the scores, coverage and notes, apply the winner:
.br
	mbsvpbest -I datalist.mb-1 -S woa_data -P decav -R 01 -O evaluation --apply-best

.SH SEE ALSO
\fBmblevitus\fP(1), \fBmbprocess\fP(1), \fBmbset\fP(1), \fBmbsvplist\fP(1),
